# Liquid stage 2 (leg 1): switch the real liquid to a MULTI-SIGMA
# Uhlenbeck-Ford fluid that actually resembles it.
#
# The analytic UF free energy exists only for a single-component fluid, and a
# single sigma forced onto an oxide melt gives a reference the liquid does not
# overlap (F then drifts with p and sigma when it must be invariant). So leg 1
# targets a per-pair-sigma UFM, and leg 2 carries that to the single-sigma
# fluid whose free energy is known.
#
# Two probed facts this template relies on: `compute pair <substyle>` returns
# the RAW substyle energy (not the scaled one), so the integrand is simply
# (U_ufm - U_real)/N; and hybrid/scaled lives in the LAMMPS core, so it is
# present in builds whose package list does not mention it.
#
# Runs NVT (Langevin on NVE): the volume is the melt-stage NPT volume, frozen
# into the input cell.
#
# Outputs: fwd.dat, bwd.dat (lambda, dU/dlambda), ufm_endpoint.data.

units metal
atom_style atomic
boundary p p p
read_data input.data

variable lam equal 0.0
variable fscale equal 1.0-v_lam
variable bscale equal v_lam
pair_style hybrid/scaled v_fscale ${pair_style} v_bscale ufm ${ufm_cutoff}
pair_coeff * * ${pair_style} ${potential_path} ${species_string}
${ufm_pair_coeffs}

timestep ${time_step}
thermo ${thermo_interval}

compute c1 all pair ${pair_style}
compute c2 all pair ufm
variable dU equal (c_c2-c_c1)/atoms
fix nve all nve
fix lan all langevin ${temperature} ${temperature} 0.1 ${seed} zero yes
run ${n_equil}

variable lam equal ramp(0,1)
fix fwd all print 50 "${lam} ${dU}" file fwd.dat screen no title "lambda dU"
run ${n_switch}
unfix fwd

variable lam equal 1.0
run ${n_equil}
write_data ufm_endpoint.data

variable lam equal ramp(1,0)
fix bwd all print 50 "${lam} ${dU}" file bwd.dat screen no title "lambda dU"
run ${n_switch}
